    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_fe8ee71322e5d66df3c8f822d5d000238c169a952a8d2c4626f1975af0f95d1a",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The source separates two limitations. Under its explicit idealization of infinite-precision arithmetic and untruncated C(n,z) Taylor series, roots counted on the critical line are genuine, yet local sampling can still miss crossings that remain within the tolerance between nearby zeros. In the actual twenty-digit implementation, input/phase error and accumulation over the main cosine sum grow with t; the quoted crossover near 6.5 million is an assumption-based estimate, not a certified or universal limit.",
