      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9c529527b19a84cb3d6c3a3b188a9051d3ff336a14daa68afa73ac3db939eb7d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Offline correction-table construction and a selectable correction count support a cheap-first evaluator: ordinary Gram tests use two correction terms, failed error-margin tests trigger five-term reevaluation and deeper partition search, while fixed-precision failure and batch precomputation belong to separate reliability and throughput regimes.",
